{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "591a6007",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 05 - Genomic Profiles, Reliability and Robustness\n",
    "\n",
    "**Questions answered here**\n",
    "- Q3. Does Proof Source influence the observed relationships? (formal interaction test)\n",
    "- Q4/Q5. Are there distinct genomic profiles? Do animals form well-separated clusters? (PCA + k-means)\n",
    "- Q6. Which animals are above the herd mean on all six subindexes?\n",
    "- Plus two robustness analyses demanded by review: TOST equivalence for milk, and\n",
    "  sire-clustered standard errors for the body-size associations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Every number in the README that comes from this notebook is produced by a cell below,\n",
    "run on the real confidential dataset. The synthetic sample in `data/` reproduces\n",
    "structure only and will NOT reproduce these findings by design.\n",
    "\n",
    "**All values are published genetic evaluations representing predicted genetic merit, not measured performance. Most are genomic evaluations, but other proof sources are present.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "13e12af8",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:29.241393Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:29.241254Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.634559Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.633511Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loaded (668, 141) | sires: 212\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import warnings; warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import pandas as pd, numpy as np\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "import statsmodels.formula.api as smf\n",
    "from statsmodels.stats.anova import anova_lm\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load real data (local). The public repo ships only data/sample_synthetic.csv,\n",
    "# which reproduces structure but NOT the correlations, so it will not reproduce results.\n",
    "hits = [p for base in [Path(\".\"),Path(\"..\"),Path(\"../..\")] if base.exists()\n",
    "        for p in base.rglob(\"Master_Database*.xlsx\")]\n",
    "df = pd.read_excel(hits[0], sheet_name=\"Data\", header=1).dropna(how=\"all\") if hits else pd.read_csv(\"../data/sample_synthetic.csv\")\n",
    "df.columns = [c.strip() for c in df.columns]\n",
    "df[\"year\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"Birth Date\"], errors=\"coerce\").dt.year\n",
    "for c in [\"STA\",\"BD\",\"HFE\",\"CW\",\"Milk (kg)\",\"HL\",\"BMR\",\"Pro$\",\"PROD\",\"REPRO\",\n",
    "          \"PROD\",\"HEALTH\",\"L-TYPE\",\"REPRO\",\"M-ABILITY\",\"ENVIRO\",\"Fat (kg)\",\"Prot (kg)\",\"BD\"]:\n",
    "    if c in df.columns: df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "df[\"SireID\"] = df[\"Sire Reg Number\"].astype(str)\n",
    "z = df[[\"STA\",\"BD\",\"HFE\",\"CW\"]].apply(lambda x:(x-x.mean())/x.std())\n",
    "df[\"SIZE\"] = z.mean(axis=1)\n",
    "print(\"Loaded\", df.shape, \"| sires:\", df[\"SireID\"].nunique())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bb37367a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**This is an exploratory equivalence sensitivity analysis**, added during review, not\n",
    "exploratory. Two margins are reported: a stricter 0.33 SD of the Milk EBV (about 177\n",
    "kg) and a lenient 0.5 SD (about 268 kg). Neither is a validated biological threshold; a\n",
    "proper margin would be set in kg from a difference the industry considers economically\n",
    "irrelevant, which requires production-economics input not available here. The margins\n",
    "are therefore descriptive anchors, and the defensible conclusion is the weaker one: no\n",
    "milk advantage was detected for larger cows."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "3f06831a",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.637141Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.636384Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.652199Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.651334Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "small mean=436.0 kg (n=199) | large mean=341.7 kg (n=188)\n",
      "difference=94.3 kg | 90% CI=[2.7, 186.0]\n",
      "Milk EBV SD=536.8 kg\n",
      "\n",
      "margin +-177 kg (0.33 SD, stricter margin): p_low=0.0000 p_high=0.0687 -> equivalent: False\n",
      "margin +-268 kg (0.5 SD, sensitivity): p_low=0.0000 p_high=0.0009 -> equivalent: True\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "q1,q3 = df[\"STA\"].quantile([.25,.75])\n",
    "sm_g = df[df[\"STA\"]<=q1][\"Milk (kg)\"].dropna()\n",
    "bg_g = df[df[\"STA\"]>=q3][\"Milk (kg)\"].dropna()\n",
    "n1,n2 = len(sm_g),len(bg_g); m1,m2 = sm_g.mean(),bg_g.mean(); diff = m1-m2\n",
    "se = np.sqrt(sm_g.var()/n1 + bg_g.var()/n2)\n",
    "dof = (sm_g.var()/n1+bg_g.var()/n2)**2/((sm_g.var()/n1)**2/(n1-1)+(bg_g.var()/n2)**2/(n2-1))\n",
    "tcrit = stats.t.ppf(0.95, dof)\n",
    "ci90 = (diff - tcrit*se, diff + tcrit*se)\n",
    "herd_sd = df[\"Milk (kg)\"].std()\n",
    "print(f\"small mean={m1:.1f} kg (n={n1}) | large mean={m2:.1f} kg (n={n2})\")\n",
    "print(f\"difference={diff:.1f} kg | 90% CI=[{ci90[0]:.1f}, {ci90[1]:.1f}]\")\n",
    "print(f\"Milk EBV SD={herd_sd:.1f} kg\\n\")\n",
    "for pct,lbl,role in [(0.33,\"0.33 SD\",\"stricter margin\"),(0.5,\"0.5 SD\",\"sensitivity\")]:\n",
    "    margin = pct*herd_sd\n",
    "    p_low = 1-stats.t.cdf((diff+margin)/se,dof); p_high=stats.t.cdf((diff-margin)/se,dof)\n",
    "    equiv = max(p_low,p_high)<0.05\n",
    "    print(f\"margin +-{margin:.0f} kg ({lbl}, {role}): p_low={p_low:.4f} p_high={p_high:.4f} \"\n",
    "          f\"-> equivalent: {equiv}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d2283bfd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** Under the stricter exploratory margin of 0.33 herd SD (about 177 kg) the groups are\n",
    "**not** equivalent (upper one-sided p = 0.069). Under the lenient 0.5 SD margin they\n",
    "are. The 90% CI of the difference is [2.7, 186.0] kg.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Honest conclusion:** no statistically detectable Milk-merit advantage was found for the larger group, and\n",
    "the difference is equivalent to zero only under a lenient margin. We therefore state\n",
    "that **no meaningful milk advantage was detected for larger cows**, and treat the\n",
    "stronger phrase \"same milk\" as supported only under the 0.5 SD margin, not established\n",
    "outright."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e6214b9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Robustness 2: sire-clustered standard errors\n",
    "\n",
    "The 668 females are not independent; many share sires. Conventional SEs assume\n",
    "independence and are therefore too small. We refit the central body-size associations\n",
    "with **standard errors clustered by sire registration number** and compare."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "d462d665",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.653989Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.653832Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.723079Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.721963Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Sire-clustered SE; adjusted models add BirthYear + ProofSource:\n",
      "outcome   n  sires  coef_unadj p_unadj  coef_adj  SE_adj   p_adj           CI95_adj\n",
      "     HL 666    212       -2.20 1.4e-15     -2.40   0.281 1.4e-17     [-2.95, -1.85]\n",
      "    BMR 666    212       -3.19 4.3e-38     -3.09   0.254 4.5e-34     [-3.58, -2.59]\n",
      "   Pro$ 666    212     -383.35 1.9e-10   -463.78  52.143 5.9e-19 [-565.98, -361.58]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "rows=[]\n",
    "for outcome in [\"HL\",\"BMR\",\"Pro$\"]:\n",
    "    d = df[[\"SIZE\",outcome,\"Sire Reg Number\",\"year\",\"Proof Source\"]].dropna().rename(columns={\"Proof Source\":\"PS\"})\n",
    "    d[\"SireID\"] = d[\"Sire Reg Number\"].astype(str)  # missing sire already dropped by dropna\n",
    "    base = smf.ols(f\"Q('{outcome}') ~ SIZE\", data=d).fit(cov_type=\"cluster\",cov_kwds={\"groups\":d[\"SireID\"]})\n",
    "    adj  = smf.ols(f\"Q('{outcome}') ~ SIZE + year + C(PS)\", data=d).fit(cov_type=\"cluster\",cov_kwds={\"groups\":d[\"SireID\"]})\n",
    "    rows.append({\"outcome\":outcome,\"n\":len(d),\"sires\":d[\"SireID\"].nunique(),\n",
    "        \"coef_unadj\":round(base.params[\"SIZE\"],2),\"p_unadj\":f\"{base.pvalues['SIZE']:.1e}\",\n",
    "        \"coef_adj\":round(adj.params[\"SIZE\"],2),\"SE_adj\":round(adj.bse[\"SIZE\"],3),\n",
    "        \"p_adj\":f\"{adj.pvalues['SIZE']:.1e}\",\n",
    "        \"CI95_adj\":f\"[{adj.conf_int().loc['SIZE',0]:.2f}, {adj.conf_int().loc['SIZE',1]:.2f}]\"})\n",
    "print(\"Sire-clustered SE; adjusted models add BirthYear + ProofSource:\")\n",
    "print(pd.DataFrame(rows).to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0e809227",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** With standard errors clustered by sire (212 sire clusters, n = 666) and birth\n",
    "year and Proof Source added as covariates to address confounding from cohort change, all\n",
    "three associations remain highly significant: SIZE vs Herd Life coef -2.40 (p = 1.4e-17),\n",
    "vs Body Maintenance -3.09 (p = 4.5e-34), vs Pro$ -463.78 (p = 5.9e-19). The body-size\n",
    "associations are not an artefact of pseudo-replication across half-sib families, nor of\n",
    "simultaneous cohort trends in size and merit. They remain associations, not causal\n",
    "effects; unmeasured confounders cannot be excluded."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1c8e5cb4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q3: does evaluation stage (GPA vs GEBV) modify the production-reproduction relationship?\n",
    "\n",
    "This tests GPA against GEBV only, the two genomically tested groups, not all four Proof Source categories (PA and EBV are too small). The question is therefore about evaluation stage among genotyped animals, not Proof Source in general.\n",
    "\n",
    "A relationship being significant in one subgroup and not another does **not** show the\n",
    "subgroups differ. We test the difference directly with an interaction term and a joint\n",
    "F-test."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "6b3a6c5c",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.724795Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.724611Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.749820Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.748642Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "n = 603, sires = 192 (SE clustered by sire)\n",
      "Interaction PROD:C(PS)[T.GPA]: coef=+0.137 95%CI=[-0.073, +0.347] p=0.2017\n",
      "-> interaction NOT significant (p=0.20 with clustered SE): the subgroups\n",
      "   do not differ significantly in the PROD-REPRO relationship.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "sub = df[df[\"Proof Source\"].isin([\"GPA\",\"GEBV\"])][\n",
    "    [\"REPRO\",\"PROD\",\"Proof Source\",\"year\",\"SireID\"]].dropna().rename(columns={\"Proof Source\":\"PS\"})\n",
    "# same standard as the size models: standard errors clustered by sire\n",
    "full = smf.ols(\"REPRO ~ PROD * C(PS) + year\", data=sub).fit(\n",
    "        cov_type=\"cluster\", cov_kwds={\"groups\":sub[\"SireID\"]})\n",
    "term=[x for x in full.params.index if \"PROD:\" in x][0]\n",
    "print(f\"n = {len(sub)}, sires = {sub['SireID'].nunique()} (SE clustered by sire)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Interaction {term}: coef={full.params[term]:+.3f} \"\n",
    "      f\"95%CI=[{full.conf_int().loc[term,0]:+.3f}, {full.conf_int().loc[term,1]:+.3f}] \"\n",
    "      f\"p={full.pvalues[term]:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"-> interaction NOT significant (p=0.20 with clustered SE): the subgroups\")\n",
    "print(\"   do not differ significantly in the PROD-REPRO relationship.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1d3ef6a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** Applying the same sire-clustered standard errors used for the size models,\n",
    "the interaction term is **not significant** (coef +0.137, 95% CI [-0.073, +0.347],\n",
    "p = 0.20; even less significant than under conventional SE). The subgroups do not differ\n",
    "significantly in the production-reproduction relationship. A relationship being\n",
    "significant within GEBV alone (r = -0.145) and not pooled (r = -0.033) does not establish\n",
    "a subgroup difference, and the formal test confirms it does not."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "64d5ec41",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4/Q5: PCA and clustering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "9095f0ae",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.752517Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:32.751512Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.231578Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.229886Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "PCA on 6 subindexes:\n",
      "  PC1: 24.1%  cum  24.1%\n",
      "  PC2: 22.3%  cum  46.4%\n",
      "  PC3: 19.4%  cum  65.8%\n",
      "  PC4: 13.1%  cum  79.0%\n",
      "  PC5: 11.4%  cum  90.4%\n",
      "  PC6:  9.6%  cum 100.0%\n",
      "  PCs for 80%: 5 of 6\n",
      "\n",
      "k-means silhouette:\n",
      "  k=2: silhouette=0.143\n",
      "  k=3: silhouette=0.146\n",
      "  k=4: silhouette=0.142\n",
      "  k=5: silhouette=0.134\n",
      "  k=6: silhouette=0.136\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n",
    "SUB=[\"PROD\",\"HEALTH\",\"L-TYPE\",\"REPRO\",\"M-ABILITY\",\"ENVIRO\"]\n",
    "X=df[SUB].dropna(); Z=((X-X.mean())/X.std()).values\n",
    "ev=np.sort(np.linalg.eigvalsh(np.cov(Z,rowvar=False)))[::-1]; cum=np.cumsum(ev)/ev.sum()\n",
    "print(\"PCA on 6 subindexes:\")\n",
    "for i in range(6): print(f\"  PC{i+1}: {ev[i]/ev.sum()*100:4.1f}%  cum {cum[i]*100:5.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(f\"  PCs for 80%: {int(np.argmax(cum>=0.8))+1} of 6\\n\")\n",
    "print(\"k-means silhouette:\")\n",
    "for k in range(2,7):\n",
    "    km=KMeans(n_clusters=k,n_init=20,random_state=42).fit(Z)\n",
    "    print(f\"  k={k}: silhouette={silhouette_score(Z,km.labels_):.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c4bec57",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** 5 of 6 principal components are needed for 80% of variance (PC1 only 24.1%):\n",
    "the six subindexes are **not redundant**. K-means silhouette never exceeds 0.146 across\n",
    "k = 2 to 6, indicating weak separation under this specification.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Interpretation, stated carefully.** Under this specification (k-means on the six\n",
    "standardized subindexes) no well-separated clusters were found and the variation is\n",
    "better described as a continuum. This does not prove no structure of any kind exists.\n",
    "PCA describes multivariate structure; it does not by itself establish genetic\n",
    "independence or predict selection response."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d774a81",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q6: animals above the herd mean on all six subindexes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "38b7c3a5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.233611Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.233314Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.242464Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.241585Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Animals above the herd mean on all six subindexes (this exploratory definition): 21 of 668 (3.1%)\n",
      "Their mean Pro$ = 1887 vs herd 1145\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "zs=(X-X.mean())/X.std()\n",
    "above_mean=(zs>0).all(axis=1)\n",
    "n_above=int(above_mean.sum())\n",
    "proq = df.loc[X.index[above_mean],\"Pro$\"].mean()\n",
    "print(f\"Animals above the herd mean on all six subindexes \"\n",
    "      f\"(this exploratory definition): {n_above} of {len(X)} ({n_above/len(X)*100:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Their mean Pro$ = {proq:.0f} vs herd {df['Pro$'].mean():.0f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7eeff769",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** Only **21 animals (3.1%)** are above the herd mean on all six subindexes\n",
    "under this exploratory definition, averaging Pro$ 1,887 vs the herd's 1,145. This is a\n",
    "descriptive count under one chosen definition, not a validated \"completeness\" class."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2cca89a0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Small vs large stature quartiles, and the elite subgroup\n",
    "\n",
    "Descriptive comparison of the bottom vs top Stature quartile, and identification of the\n",
    "subgroup combining high production, adequate reproduction and below-average size."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "24e8e04f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.244252Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.244031Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.274233Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.273121Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "  Milk (kg)  small=  436.0 large=  341.7 diff= +94.3 (MWU p=1.3e-01)\n",
      "  Fat (kg)   small=   50.2 large=   30.9 diff= +19.3 (MWU p=1.4e-08)\n",
      "  Prot (kg)  small=   30.0 large=   19.1 diff= +10.9 (MWU p=3.2e-07)\n",
      "  HL         small=  103.9 large=  100.3 diff=  +3.6 (MWU p=2.4e-22)\n",
      "\n",
      "  Elite subgroup (top-quartile PROD + REPRO>=500 + below-avg size):\n",
      "    n=45 (6.7%), mean Pro$=2146 vs herd 1145\n",
      "  Body Depth cohort slope: +0.267/yr (p=0.0003)\n",
      "  REPRO herd mean: 486\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "q1,q3=df[\"STA\"].quantile([.25,.75]); sm=df[df[\"STA\"]<=q1]; bg=df[df[\"STA\"]>=q3]\n",
    "for c in [\"Milk (kg)\",\"Fat (kg)\",\"Prot (kg)\",\"HL\"]:\n",
    "    a=sm[c].dropna(); b=bg[c].dropna(); u,p=stats.mannwhitneyu(a,b)\n",
    "    print(f\"  {c:10s} small={a.mean():7.1f} large={b.mean():7.1f} diff={a.mean()-b.mean():+6.1f} (MWU p={p:.1e})\")\n",
    "p75=df[\"PROD\"].quantile(.75)\n",
    "elite=df[(df[\"PROD\"]>=p75)&(df[\"REPRO\"]>=500)&(df[\"SIZE\"]<0)]\n",
    "print(f\"\\n  Elite subgroup (top-quartile PROD + REPRO>=500 + below-avg size):\")\n",
    "print(f\"    n={len(elite)} ({len(elite)/len(df)*100:.1f}%), mean Pro$={elite['Pro$'].mean():.0f} vs herd {df['Pro$'].mean():.0f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Body Depth cohort slope: \", end=\"\")\n",
    "bd=df[df.year>=2018].groupby('year')['BD'].mean().dropna(); r=stats.linregress(bd.index,bd.values)\n",
    "print(f\"{r.slope:+.3f}/yr (p={r.pvalue:.4f})\")\n",
    "print(f\"  REPRO herd mean: {df['REPRO'].mean():.0f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "28b8988c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** Small vs large quartiles: Fat +19.3 kg, Protein +10.9 kg, Herd Life +3.6, no\n",
    "significant milk difference. The elite subgroup (high PROD + REPRO>=500 + below-average\n",
    "size) contains 45 animals (6.7%) averaging Pro$ 2,146 vs the herd's 1,145. Body Depth\n",
    "rose +0.267/yr (p=0.0003) across cohorts; REPRO herd mean is 486, below the proven-sire\n",
    "base of 500. These are descriptive within-herd figures."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "20f2ddb4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Adjusted models for Milk, Fat and Protein vs body size\n",
    "\n",
    "The Pearson correlations in notebook 03 are unadjusted. Here the composite is tested\n",
    "against Milk, Fat and Protein merit with birth year and Proof Source as covariates and\n",
    "standard errors clustered by sire (n=666), and the composite's robustness is checked by\n",
    "leave-one-out."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "b723171d",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.276741Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.275844Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.398946Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-29T02:45:33.397851Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Adjusted (SIZE + birth year + Proof Source), sire-clustered SE, n=666:\n",
      "  Milk (kg)  coef=   -9.62 95%CI=[-83.9,+64.7] p=0.8\n",
      "  Fat (kg)   coef=  -13.38 95%CI=[-17.4,-9.4] p=6.6e-11\n",
      "  Prot (kg)  coef=   -7.02 95%CI=[-10.2,-3.8] p=1.5e-05\n",
      "\n",
      "SIZE composite leave-one-out vs Fat (adjusted+clustered):\n",
      "  all four         coef=-13.38 p=6.6e-11\n",
      "  drop STA         coef=-9.74 p=5e-07\n",
      "  drop BD          coef=-14.67 p=1.3e-11\n",
      "  drop HFE         coef=-9.06 p=1.2e-05\n",
      "  drop CW          coef=-15.21 p=1.6e-18\n",
      "  Chest Width only coef=-0.27 p=0.87\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dfc = df[df[\"Sire Reg Number\"].notna()].copy()\n",
    "dfc[\"SireID\"] = dfc[\"Sire Reg Number\"].astype(str)\n",
    "zc = dfc[[\"STA\",\"BD\",\"HFE\",\"CW\"]].apply(lambda x:(x-x.mean())/x.std()); dfc[\"SIZE\"]=zc.mean(axis=1)\n",
    "for c in [\"Milk (kg)\",\"Fat (kg)\",\"Prot (kg)\"]: dfc[c]=pd.to_numeric(dfc[c],errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "print(\"Adjusted (SIZE + birth year + Proof Source), sire-clustered SE, n=666:\")\n",
    "for out in [\"Milk (kg)\",\"Fat (kg)\",\"Prot (kg)\"]:\n",
    "    d=dfc[[\"SIZE\",out,\"SireID\",\"year\",\"Proof Source\"]].dropna().rename(columns={\"Proof Source\":\"PS\"})\n",
    "    m=smf.ols(f\"Q('{out}') ~ SIZE + year + C(PS)\",data=d).fit(cov_type=\"cluster\",cov_kwds={\"groups\":d[\"SireID\"]})\n",
    "    ci=m.conf_int().loc[\"SIZE\"]\n",
    "    print(f\"  {out:10s} coef={m.params['SIZE']:+8.2f} 95%CI=[{ci[0]:+.1f},{ci[1]:+.1f}] p={m.pvalues['SIZE']:.2g}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nSIZE composite leave-one-out vs Fat (adjusted+clustered):\")\n",
    "for name,cc in [(\"all four\",[\"STA\",\"BD\",\"HFE\",\"CW\"]),(\"drop STA\",[\"BD\",\"HFE\",\"CW\"]),\n",
    "                (\"drop BD\",[\"STA\",\"HFE\",\"CW\"]),(\"drop HFE\",[\"STA\",\"BD\",\"CW\"]),(\"drop CW\",[\"STA\",\"BD\",\"HFE\"]),\n",
    "                (\"Chest Width only\",[\"CW\"])]:\n",
    "    zz=dfc[cc].apply(lambda x:(x-x.mean())/x.std()); dfc[\"Stmp\"]=zz.mean(axis=1)\n",
    "    d=dfc[[\"Stmp\",\"Fat (kg)\",\"SireID\",\"year\",\"Proof Source\"]].dropna().rename(columns={\"Proof Source\":\"PS\"})\n",
    "    m=smf.ols(\"Q('Fat (kg)') ~ Stmp + year + C(PS)\",data=d).fit(cov_type=\"cluster\",cov_kwds={\"groups\":d[\"SireID\"]})\n",
    "    print(f\"  {name:16s} coef={m.params['Stmp']:+.2f} p={m.pvalues['Stmp']:.2g}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "99cc7d4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Result.** After adjustment, the composite is unrelated to Milk merit (coef -9.6, 95% CI\n",
    "[-83.9, +64.7], p = 0.80) and negatively related to Fat (coef -13.4, p = 7e-11) and\n",
    "Protein (coef -7.0, p = 2e-05). The adjusted null for Milk strengthens the \"no milk\n",
    "association\" reading over the raw correlation. Leave-one-out shows the negative Fat\n",
    "association holds under every composite except Chest Width alone (null), so the result is\n",
    "not driven by any single component; Chest Width contributes least. These remain\n",
    "associations among published evaluations in one herd, adjusted for cohort and proof source\n",
    "but not for the full relationship structure; they are not genetic correlations or causal\n",
    "effects."
   ]
  }
 ],
